k to per-input. Edge cases (UTF-8 multibyte, end-of-string, span crossing separator) all have direct test coverage in `TestCharToByteOffset` / `TestPartitionIndex`.\n- **Error hygiene.** `RedactBatch` deliberately omits stdout/stderr content from error strings (OPF could echo input fragments when misconfigured). Asserted by `TestShellOut_ExitError_DoesNotLeakStderr` and `TestShellOut_ParseError_DoesNotLeakStdout`. Good defense.\n- **`WaitDelay: 500ms`** on `*exec.Cmd` ensures `cmd.Wait()` returns promptly when descendant processes hold pipes after a kill. Comment explains the Linux-CI motivation — non-obvious detail worth keeping.\n- **`validateOPFSettings` rejects unknown category names at parse time.** Silent zero-detection of a privacy category would let a typo make a user think they're protected. `DisallowUnknownFields` + this check together also pin `on_failure` as nonexistent (tested explicitly).\n- **`DisallowUnknownFields` round-trip** with category validation is covered on both the `LoadFromBytes` and merge paths. `TestLoadFromBytes_OPFSettings_Merge` exercises override semantics correctly.\n\n### Issues worth addressing\n\n**1. Test-only helpers are part of the public package API.**\n`GetOPFConfigForTest` and `ResetOPFConfigForTest` are exported in `redact/opf.go`. Idiomatic Go puts these in an `export_test.go` (still `package redact`) so they're only visible to tests within the package. Today, any consumer of `github.com/entireio/cli/redact` can call them — risk is small but the API surface is wider than intended.\n\n**2. Subtle behavioral change in `finalizeAllTurnCheckpoints` prompt redaction is not type-enforced.**\n`manual_commit_hooks.go:2728-2756` — the old code mutated `prompts[i] = redact.String(p)` in place, then passed redacted prompts to `UpdateCommittedOptions.Prompts`. The new code leaves `prompts` UNREDACTED and supplies the redacted blob via `PromptsRedactedContent`. The writer (`committed.go:writeSessionToSubdirectory`) currently only uses