age gap: no integration test asserting OPF's `\"secret\"` label produces bare `REDACTED`.**\nThe `opfLabelMap[\"secret\"] = \"\"` mapping → `applyRegions` → `replacementToken(\"\")` returns bare `REDACTED`. The single-string test `TestStringWithPrivacyFilter_AugmentsRegexLayers` covers PERSON. Worth adding a case that exercises the empty-label branch — it's a real product behavior (secrets render as `REDACTED`, not `[REDACTED_SECRET]`) and currently untested via the OPF path.\n\n**8. `JSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter` happy-path assertion missing.**\n`TestJSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter_BatchesSingleCall` asserts the batch count is 1; `TestJSONLContentWithPrivacyFilter_FallsBackOnBatchError` asserts non-empty output on fallback. No test checks that the returned content actually contains the redaction tokens for an OPF-tagged leaf. Easy to add and increases confidence that Pass 3's per-leaf \"regex layers + cached OPF spans\" path produces the right bytes.\n\n**9. `\\x1e` collision risk in inputs.**\nThe comment says U+001E \"doesn't appear in real text.\" True for almost all transcripts, but not guaranteed for tool output or user prompts. If a leaf legitimately contains `\\x1e`, the `partitionIndex` could miscount (a span starting before the embedded `\\x1e` would still fit within its input's bounds, so usually fine; spans crossing it are dropped silently). Acceptable as v1 — but worth noting in a comment that this is a defensive-best-effort assumption.\n\n### Correctness sanity-check\n\n- **Byte/rune offset translation**: `RedactBatch` does `strings.ReplaceAll(in, \"\\n\", \" \")` before joining. Newlines and spaces are both 1 byte → byte offsets stay valid. Slicing the original `v` with these offsets in Pass 3 is safe. ✓\n- **Bounds check in Pass 3**: `sp.End > len(v)` filters out OPF spans that exceed the input. Original-input length == flattened-input length (1-byte substitution), so the check is sound. ✓\n- **Concurrent first failures**: `opfBreakerTripped.CompareAndSwap(false, true)` ensures only one of N concurrent first-failures prints the warning. ✓\n\n### Performance\n\nThe PR's own description quantifies it: ~25–30s of OPF inference per commit on a real-world transcript (one batched shell-out for the transcript + one for the joined prompts), plus the per-turn pipeline is untouched. Reasonable tradeoff for opt-in PII detection. The `PromptsRedactedContent` short-circuit on multi-checkpoint commits is exactly the right optimization — without it, an N-checkpoint commit would pay N× the joined-prompt OPF call.\n\n### Security\n\n- Stdout/stderr redaction in error messages: correct.\n- No content leakage via slog: the `handleOPFFailure` slog call passes only `cfg.Command` and `err.Error()` — both bytes-only.\n- Settings parse path uses `DisallowUnknownFields` and validates category names; misconfiguration fails closed.\n\n### Recommendation\n\n**Approve with minor follow-ups.** The architecture is correct, the test coverage is thoughtful (especially the \"plain entry points never invoke OPF\" regression test), and the privacy/security considerations have been handled carefully. The items above are nits and small coverage additions — none are blockers. Items #1 (move test helpers to `export_test.go`) and #2 (compile-time-enforce or document the `Prompts`/`PromptsRedactedContent` invariant) are the two I'd actually do in a follow-up.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The `*ForTest`/`*WithRuntime` naming convention for test-only entry points is a reasonable middle ground when you don't want to use `export_test.go` — the suffix tells consumers \"don't call this from production code.\" Go's tooling won't enforce it, but `golangci-lint` with `forbidigo` could.\n- The pattern of \"use the type system to enforce invariants\" (the existing `RedactedBytes` wrapper) was applied for the transcript path but NOT for the prompts path. Worth thinking about whether `PromptsRedactedContent` should be a typed `RedactedBytes`/`RedactedString` rather than a bare `string` — it would catch issue #2 at compile time.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3813,"cache_read_input_tokens":132887,"output_tokens":4406,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3813,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4406,"cache_read_input_tokens":132887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3813},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4YuHraT5zh8G1nTc6Z6","attributionSkill":"review","type":"assistant","uuid":"c1d1d9e1-019b-425a-b53b-2b41c05b5fcd","timestamp":"2026-05-15T14:58:47.964Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"82b06be1-eb40-429b-b82b-fc441eac5e42","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
