{"parentUuid":"9618c208-13c6-4142-8ba8-f85a5e078270","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WCU3uXBSZVx12Ax4yPd4dG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- Moving OPF from post-commit to pre-push is the real performance win here, more than the prompt itself. Commits happen many times an hour; pushes maybe a few times. Same OPF cost, paid much less often.\n- The prompt is gravy — once OPF only fires at push, users naturally pay attention to it because they actively chose to push.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nConcretely, what this turns into:\n\n**Architecture shift (the real work)**: today OPF runs at post-commit condensation, so the bytes on `entire/checkpoints/v1` are already OPF-redacted before push. Moving to pre-push means:\n1. Post-commit writes checkpoints with the 7-layer pipeline only\n2. Pre-push hook (`manual_commit_hooks.go` PrePush path) identifies unpushed `entire/checkpoints/v1` commits, runs OPF over their trees, rewrites them as new commits, pushes the new tip\n3. Local branch fast-forwards to the rewritten tip\n\nThis is a non-trivial change to the pre-push flow but architecturally clean — checkpoint commit SHAs aren't referenced from anywhere else (user commits link by 12-hex `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer to tree paths, not SHAs), so rewriting is safe.\n\n**Prompt layer (the UX)**: in the pre-push hook, before launching OPF:\n- TTY: `huh` form with options `Yes / No / Always (this push)` — wired through `NewAccessibleForm`\n- Non-interactive (no TTY): print `→ OpenAI Privacy Filter: scanning N checkpoints (may take 30s+)…` and proceed (matches your \"if enabled, just print\" preference)\n- CLI flag: `entire push --opf=yes|no|always` to override the prompt non-interactively for scripts\n- Settings: keep `redaction.openai_privacy_filter.enabled` as-is; optionally add `prompt_default: \"ask\"|\"always\"|\"never\"` if you want a sticky default\n\n**Want me to write this up as a plan first** (concrete commit boundaries, files touched, test plan) before touching code, or jump straight to implementation? Given the architectural piece, I'd lean toward a written plan."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3725,"cache_read_input_tokens":244113,"output_tokens":5291,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3725,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":5291,"cache_read_input_tokens":244113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3725,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3725},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cb4fet6W7aq9vBKfQ5H9b","type":"assistant","uuid":"2305b442-c6b7-4bc9-b50e-1fc4892ce006","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:27:31.427Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/redact-2","sessionId":"82b06be1-eb40-429b-b82b-fc441eac5e42","version":"2.1.141","gitBranch":"redact-2"}
